# Question 4: Consecutive Login Days

This is common in product companies.

---

## Example

| user | day |
| ---- | --- |
| A    | 1   |
| A    | 2   |
| A    | 3   |

---

Need:

```text
Users who logged in consecutive days
```

---

## Idea

Use:

```sql
LAG()
```

to compare current row with previous row.

---

### Simplified Query

```sql
SELECT user_id,
       login_date,
       LAG(login_date)
       OVER(
          PARTITION BY user_id
          ORDER BY login_date
       ) prev_date
FROM logins;
```

---

Then compare:

```text
Current date - Previous date = 1 day
```

---

## Recognition Pattern

Question says:

```text
Previous row
Next row
Consecutive
Trend
```

Think:

```text
LAG
LEAD
```

